meta {
  name: Delete Asset (Undeclared)
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

delete {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/assets/REPLACE_WITH_ASSET_ID
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08 against a throwaway asset (id
  `6aa0220a2b6fd055ffb7caa1`, since deleted) -- **not** the kept fixture.

  `openapi_pimv3.json` declares `GET`/`PATCH` for `/assets/{identifier}`
  but explicitly **no `DELETE`** -- `TESTING_PLAN.md` flagged this as
  worth confirming empirically rather than assuming it's a real gap.
  Confirmed it works exactly like every Phase 1 resource: `204 No
  Content`, and a follow-up `GET` on the same id then returns `404`. This
  is the 7th resource this session/last where undeclared `DELETE` was
  found working -- see `config/api-testing.config.md` quirk #20 for the
  running tally.
}
